21-Q35 = 15/35 = 42.9% ≥ 30% ✓\n- Sample answers for scenarios: Q21-Q25 have sample answers; Q26-Q35 also have sample answers ✓\n\nC01 looks complete. Now checking C02: it has 10 MCQs in Section A, 5 short answers in Section B, and 3 structured questions in Section C, but it's missing the Q-format question bank entirely and none of the questions have CoCU reference codes. This means C02 fails the 40+ question requirement and lacks the proper tagging structure.\n\nI need to add a complete Q-format section to C02 following the same pattern as C01, which means building out roughly 14 BMS theory questions, 14 HV cable systems questions, and 12 OBC questions across MCQ, graded scenarios, and enrichment scenarios, plus a 25-mark answer key.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the distribution across question types — 6 graded scenarios and 6 enrichment scenarios will give me the 30% scenario coverage I need, with the remaining questions as MCQs. I should also verify the existing Section A answer key in C02 and make sure the new Q-format questions align with the same rigor level.\n\nLooking at how C01 structures its exam, I see it combines the traditional Section A/B/C format with a separate Q-format section. I'll follow that same approach for C02, adding the Q-format questions while keeping the original sections intact. The Q-format section will start with 28 multiple choice questions covering the three content areas proportionally. I'm settling on a consistent structure: 20 multiple-choice questions worth 20 marks covering the core topics, then 5-6 graded scenario questions for another 5 marks, with enrichment questions at zero marks to reach the 25-mark total across 35-40 questions.\n\nFor the content distribution, I'm allocating roughly equal weight to BMS theory and HV cable systems at about 35% each, with OBC taking up the remaining 30%, then mapping these across the question sections so the early MCQs hit the foundational material while later sections blend in the applied scenari