oCU C02.4.1\nQ10. Main positive contactor opens when — CoCU C02.3.2\nQ11. Minimum personnel for battery pack removal — 3 (per existing C02 KA.md answer) — CoCU C02.4.2\nQ12. HV cable insulation resistance must exceed — 1 MΩ (per existing answers) — CoCU C02.3.3\nQ13. Lockout-Tagout (LOTO) purpose — prevent accidental re-energisation — CoCU C02.4.1\nQ14. Pre-charge sequence timing — 0.5-2 seconds — CoCU C02.2.3\n\nNow moving into the OBC section, starting with what the onboard charger converts...\n\nAC to DC for charging — CoCU C02.5.1. The DC-DC converter essentially replaces the alternator function found in traditional ICE vehicles — CoCU C02.6.1. Its normal output sits at 13.5-14.4V — CoCU C02.6.2. For input, the OBC can handle single-phase at 6.6kW or three-phase at 22kW — CoCU C02.5.2, and it uses liquid cooling for thermal management — CoCU C02.5.3. When dealing with defective battery modules, they need to be stored below 30% SOC before disposal — CoCU C02.4.3.\n\nMoving into the graded scenarios now. Q21 covers a BMS cell voltage deviation scenario — CoCU C02.2.2 / C02.2.4. Q22 involves a pre-charge timeout fault — CoCU C02.2.3. Q23 presents a damaged orange HV cable scenario.\n\nQ23 involves a damaged orange HV cable — CoCU C02.3.1 / C02.3.3. Q24 deals with a missing interlock connector — CoCU C02.4.1. Q25 is an OBC charging fault code scenario — CoCU C02.5.3.\n\nNow into the enrichment section. For BMS theory, I'm looking at cell balancing methods comparing passive and active approaches — CoCU C02.2.2. Then the CMU communication protocol — CoCU C02.2.1, thermal runaway mechanisms — CoCU C02.1.3, and the distinction between SOH and SOC — CoCU C02.2.1. Battery pack configuration effects with series and parallel arrangements — CoCU C02.1.2.\n\nFor HV cable systems enrichment, I'm covering the six-step Lockout-Tagout procedure — CoCU C02.4.1, cable routing specifications including bend radius and segregation rules — CoCU C02.3.1, service plug replacement steps — CoCU C02.4.1, main contactor weld failure symptoms and diagnosis — CoCU C02.3.2, and zero-energy verification adapted for this module — CoCU C02.3.3 / C02.4.1.\n\nFor OBC enrichment, I'm examining the power factor correction circuit — CoCU C02.5.1, and the next question appears to be cut off.\n\nNow I need to develop the actual sample answers for the scenario questions, each requiring at least 50 words. The marking structure is 25 marks total with Section A covering Q1-Q20, Section B with Q21-Q25 at one mark each, and Section C as enrichment with no marks. I'm planning to modify the C01 knowledge area file to ensure comprehensive coverage.\n\nLooking back at the acceptance criteria, I notice the reference format needs adjustment — the examples show `CoCU C01.3.2 - HV Safety Procedures` with a hyphen and description, but the current questions use `[CoCU C01.1.2]` without the descriptive text. That formatting inconsistency might be what caused issues before. I should verify the grep pattern matches the correct reference structure across both C01 and C02 files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2049,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9001,"cache_read_input_tokens":33820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9001},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"794df4fc-0917-40f0-aba2-b2d02fc662d7","uuid":"11571cb5-3351-4cef-a096-d341e36045a7"}
